*.sln.docstates
*.swp
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/

# ...but Android's build-type source sets are SOURCE, not build output. `src/debug/` and
# `src/release/` are where a Gradle build type overrides a resource, and the debug one carries the
# only copy of the development network allowlist. The rules above are written for .NET's bin/Debug,
# and they swallowed it: the file existed on every machine it had been made on and on no other, so a
# fresh clone built a debug APK that could not reach a local API at all.
!Khadra.Mobile/android/app/src/debug/
!Khadra.Mobile/android/app/src/release/
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
.vs/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
packages/
*.deps.json
*.runtimeconfig.json
*.runtimeconfig.dev.json

